<title>INDIA: India's IPCL 1996/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>India's IPCL 1996/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     5,102.0   vs   6,036.9</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	    4.0   vs	 4.0</p>
<p>    Gross sales	   34,300.0   vs  38,040.0</p>
<p>    Net Sales	     27,850.0   vs  31,028.4</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	   20.56  vs	24.13</p>
<p>    Gross profit	   7,410.00  vs  10,920.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   1,480.0   vs   1,220.0</p>
<p>    Tax			  830.0   vs   3,660.0</p>
<p>Note: Indian Petrochemicals Corporation Ltd. is India's leading integrated petrochemicals maker. The firm said lower import tariffs and depressed international prices of chemicals and petrochemicals affected sales realisations.</p>
<p>The hike in fuel and raw materials led to increased expenses, IPCL said. The firm said it produced 705,908 tonnes of petrochemicals during the year.</p>
<p>IPCL raised $175 million through a Euro-convertible bond issue last February.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
